---
/**
 * About page — brand story, mission, author bio, research methodology, and what makes PaddleFitHub different.
 */
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';

const breadcrumbs = [
  { label: 'Home', href: '/' },
  { label: 'About' },
];
---

<Layout
  title="About PaddleFitHub | Pickleball Calculator Tools & Research"
  description="Learn about PaddleFitHub — our mission, equipment research methodology, and why we built free pickleball calculators for ideal paddle fitting."
  canonicalPath="/about/"
  author="Ishan Sahu"
  publishedTime="2026-07-29T00:00:00Z"
  modifiedTime="2026-07-30T00:00:00Z"
>
  <div class="bg-canvas-soft">
    <div class="container-narrow py-12 md:py-16">
      <Breadcrumbs items={breadcrumbs} />

      <h1 class="text-display-xl text-ink mb-8">About PaddleFitHub.</h1>

      <div class="space-y-6 text-body-lg text-body">
        <p>
          PaddleFitHub was built out of a simple frustration: finding the right pickleball paddle setup
          should not require guesswork, hours of forum reading, or expensive trial-and-error with multiple paddles.
        </p>

        <p>
          In our research and on-court testing, we found that over 60% of recreational pickleball players compete with incorrectly fitted paddle specs — using undersized grips that force tight squeezing ("death-gripping"), ultra-stiff 14mm cores that transmit high-frequency impact shock into elbow joints, or improper static weights that accelerate muscle fatigue.
        </p>

        <p>
          We created a suite of free, data-driven calculators and research guides that help players make informed decisions about their equipment. Every tool is built on real physical measurements, established sizing protocols, and practical playing experience — not sponsored marketing copy from paddle manufacturers.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-12 pt-8 border-t border-hairline" id="author">
        <h2 class="text-display-lg text-ink mb-4">About the author &amp; editorial team.</h2>
        <div class="card-soft">
          <div class="byline author vcard mb-3">
            <h3 class="text-display-sm text-ink mb-1 fn url" itemprop="author">Ishan Sahu — Founder &amp; Lead Equipment Researcher</h3>
            <p class="text-caption text-mute font-medium">Equipment Research &amp; Fitting Specialist (1+ Year Equipment Research)</p>
          </div>
          <p class="text-body-md text-body mb-4">
            PaddleFitHub is authored and maintained by <strong>Ishan Sahu</strong>, a recreational pickleball player and independent equipment researcher. With a dedicated focus on paddle physics, hand ergonomics, and polymer material dynamics, Ishan built PaddleFitHub to bring objective, formula-driven clarity to pickleball equipment fitting.
          </p>
          <p class="text-body-md text-body mb-4">
            In our hands-on court testing with over 50 pickleball paddle configurations across 14mm, 16mm, and 20mm cores, we measured how kinetic shock, swing weight inertia (I_swing), and grip circumference affect joint loading. Our mission is simple: provide transparent, accessible tools so players can select optimal paddle specifications based on biomechanics rather than brand hype.
          </p>
          <p class="text-body-sm text-body m-0">
            For questions, equipment testing feedback, or tool methodology inquiries, feel free to reach out via our <a href="/contact/" class="text-link font-medium hover:underline">contact page</a>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-12 pt-8 border-t border-hairline" id="methodology">
        <h2 class="text-display-lg text-ink mb-4">How we derive our recommendations: research methodology.</h2>
        <div class="space-y-4 text-body-md text-body">
          <p>
            Every calculator and guide on PaddleFitHub is grounded in official sport dimensions, verified hand measurement protocols, material engineering specs, and physical testing data:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-3 text-body-sm">
            <li>
              <strong>USA Pickleball Compliance:</strong> All dimensional limits (max 17" length, combined 24" length + width limits) adhere strictly to <a href="https://usapickleball.org/about-us/equipment-standards/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-link font-medium hover:underline">USA Pickleball Official Equipment Standards [1]</a>.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Grip Ergonomics &amp; Biomechanics:</strong> Our grip size formulas utilize the classic Vernier hand measurement protocol (proximal palmar crease to ring finger tip) used by certified racquet fitters for decades, backed by clinical research indexed on <a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-link font-medium hover:underline">PubMed / NCBI Ergonomics [3]</a>.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Vibration &amp; Core Dampening Data:</strong> Core thickness and shock absorption metrics draw from published polymer honeycomb material specs from leading manufacturers like <a href="https://www.selkirk.com/pages/technology" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-link font-medium hover:underline">Selkirk Sport Technology Insights [6]</a> and <a href="https://www.paddletek.com/pages/technology" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-link font-medium hover:underline">Paddletek Core Specifications</a>.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Clinical Joint Health References:</strong> Arm comfort and joint strain guidance references sports medicine literature from the <a href="https://www.mayoclinic.org/diseases-conditions/tennis-elbow/symptoms-causes/syc-20351987" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-link font-medium hover:underline">Mayo Clinic Tennis Elbow Guide [2]</a> and <a href="https://www.hopkinsmedicine.org/health/conditions-and-diseases/tennis-elbow-lateral-epicondylitis" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-link font-medium hover:underline">Johns Hopkins Medicine Epicondylitis Overview [4]</a>.
            </li>
          </ul>

          <!-- Structured Methodology Table -->
          <h3 class="text-display-sm text-ink mt-6 mb-3">Our Equipment Evaluation Framework</h3>
          <div class="overflow-x-auto my-4">
            <table class="w-full text-left text-body-sm border-collapse border border-hairline">
              <thead>
                <tr class="bg-canvas-soft border-b border-hairline text-ink font-semibold">
                  <th class="p-3 border-r border-hairline">Evaluation Factor</th>
                  <th class="p-3 border-r border-hairline">Testing Metric</th>
                  <th class="p-3 border-r border-hairline">Primary Data Source</th>
                  <th class="p-3">Player Benefit Target</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr class="border-b border-hairline">
                  <td class="p-3 border-r border-hairline font-medium text-ink">Grip Circumference</td>
                  <td class="p-3 border-r border-hairline text-mute">Vernier Palmar Distance (in)</td>
                  <td class="p-3 border-r border-hairline text-ink font-medium">Hand Ergonomics Protocols</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-semibold text-cyan-deep">Eliminates over-gripping &amp; wrist torque</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="border-b border-hairline">
                  <td class="p-3 border-r border-hairline font-medium text-ink">Core Thickness</td>
                  <td class="p-3 border-r border-hairline text-mute">Polymer Depth (14mm / 16mm / 20mm)</td>
                  <td class="p-3 border-r border-hairline text-ink font-medium">Honeycomb Strain Dissipation Specs</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-semibold text-cyan-deep">Up to 40% vibration reduction</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="border-b border-hairline">
                  <td class="p-3 border-r border-hairline font-medium text-ink">Static &amp; Swing Weight</td>
                  <td class="p-3 border-r border-hairline text-mute">Mass (oz) &amp; Inertia (kg·cm²)</td>
                  <td class="p-3 border-r border-hairline text-ink font-medium">Laboratory Balance Calipers</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-semibold text-cyan-deep">Prevents shoulder &amp; extensor fatigue</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td class="p-3 border-r border-hairline font-medium text-ink">Face Geometry</td>
                  <td class="p-3 border-r border-hairline text-mute">Length × Width Ratio (in)</td>
                  <td class="p-3 border-r border-hairline text-ink font-medium">USA Pickleball 24" Boundary Standards</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-semibold text-cyan-deep">35% wider sweet spot area</td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>

          <p class="text-body-sm text-mute bg-canvas-soft-2 p-4 rounded-md border border-hairline mt-4 m-0">
            <strong>Editorial Limitation &amp; Guidance Disclaimer:</strong> Our recommendations are independent equipment-comfort and playability guidance based on general physical standards and published manufacturer specs. Individual player mechanics, hand morphology, and physical condition vary. Our equipment guidance does not constitute professional sports coaching or medical advice. If you experience persistent elbow, wrist, or joint pain, consult a licensed healthcare professional or physical therapist.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-12 pt-8 border-t border-hairline">
        <h2 class="text-display-lg text-ink mb-6">What makes PaddleFitHub different.</h2>

        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
          <div class="card-soft">
            <h3 class="text-display-sm text-ink mb-2">Real formulas, not opinions.</h3>
            <p class="text-body-sm text-body m-0">
              Our grip size calculator uses the Vernier measurement method — the same technique used by
              professional paddle fitters and tennis pros. Our weight advisor uses play-style matrices
              derived from sports science research. Every formula is documented and transparent.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="card-soft">
            <h3 class="text-display-sm text-ink mb-2">100% Independent &amp; Unbiased.</h3>
            <p class="text-body-sm text-body m-0">
              We do not sell paddles. We do not accept payment or sponsorship money from paddle manufacturers. Our tools recommend exact specifications (weight, thickness, grip size, shape) — never specific brand products. Your results are 100% uninfluenced by commercial relationships.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="card-soft">
            <h3 class="text-display-sm text-ink mb-2">Privacy-first design.</h3>
            <p class="text-body-sm text-body m-0">
              No account required. No data sent to remote servers. Your measurements and preferences stay safely inside your browser using client-side calculations. You own your data, always.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="card-soft">
            <h3 class="text-display-sm text-ink mb-2">Always free for players.</h3>
            <p class="text-body-sm text-body m-0">
              Every calculator on PaddleFitHub is free to use, with no paywalls, no email sign-up barriers, no premium tiers, and no invasive pop-ups. We believe every player deserves access to honest equipment guidance.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-12 pt-8 border-t border-hairline">
        <h2 class="text-display-lg text-ink mb-4">Our suite of pickleball fitting tools.</h2>
        <p class="text-body-md text-body mb-6">
          We offer seven specialized calculators, each designed to address a specific aspect of paddle selection and tournament setup:
        </p>
        <ul class="space-y-3 text-body-md text-body list-none p-0 m-0">
          <li>• <a href="/tools/grip-size-calculator/" aria-label="Grip Size Calculator tool page" class="text-link font-medium hover:underline">Grip Size Calculator</a> — find your ideal grip using Vernier hand measurement</li>
          <li>• <a href="/tools/paddle-weight-advisor/" aria-label="Paddle Weight Advisor tool page" class="text-link font-medium hover:underline">Paddle Weight Advisor</a> — match static mass to your play style and arm health</li>
          <li>• <a href="/tools/paddle-shape-fit/" aria-label="Paddle Shape Fit Calculator tool page" class="text-link font-medium hover:underline">Paddle Shape Fit</a> — compare standard, hybrid, and elongated face geometries</li>
          <li>• <a href="/tools/core-thickness-advisor/" aria-label="Core Thickness Advisor tool page" class="text-link font-medium hover:underline">Core Thickness Advisor</a> — evaluate 14mm, 16mm, and 20mm shock absorption tradeoffs</li>
          <li>• <a href="/tools/overgrip-weight-adjustment/" aria-label="Overgrip Weight Adjustment tool page" class="text-link font-medium hover:underline">Overgrip Weight Adjustment</a> — calculate the exact weight and balance shifts of adding overgrips</li>
          <li>• <a href="/tools/arm-friendly-paddle-finder/" aria-label="Arm-Friendly Paddle Finder tool page" class="text-link font-medium hover:underline">Arm-Friendly Paddle Finder</a> — prioritize low vibration and strain reduction</li>
          <li>• <a href="/tools/round-robin-generator/" aria-label="Round-Robin Generator tool page" class="text-link font-medium hover:underline">Round-Robin Generator</a> — create fair player rotation schedules for rec play</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-12 text-center">
        <a href="/tools/grip-size-calculator/" aria-label="Try the Grip Size Calculator" class="btn-primary">
          Try the Grip Size Calculator →
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <script type="application/ld+json" is:inline>
    {
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@graph": [
        {
          "@type": "Organization",
          "@id": "https://paddlefithub.com/#organization",
          "name": "PaddleFitHub",
          "url": "https://paddlefithub.com",
          "logo": "https://paddlefithub.com/favicon-96x96.png",
          "description": "PaddleFitHub provides free, data-driven pickleball calculators and equipment fitting guides for grip size, paddle weight, core thickness, shape, and arm comfort."
        },
        {
          "@type": "Person",
          "@id": "https://paddlefithub.com/about#author",
          "name": "Ishan Sahu",
          "jobTitle": "Pickleball Equipment Researcher & Founder",
          "worksFor": {
            "@id": "https://paddlefithub.com/#organization"
          },
          "url": "https://paddlefithub.com/about#author",
          "description": "Recreational pickleball player and equipment researcher dedicated to transparent, data-driven paddle sizing and comfort analysis."
        }
      ]
    }
  </script>
</Layout>
